WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.940
"A mystical potion
that cures all diseases."

2
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.480
It's magic. so there's a decent
chance that includes Eternal Sleep.

3
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.120
It only takes three ingredients
to craft this Elixir of Life.

4
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.280
While I don't have any of them yet.

5
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.960
I do know exactly where they are.

6
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:38.210
But going back to that castle
as I am now is a death wish.

7
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.510
I need to level up more.

8
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.590
Stronger.

9
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.020
I need to get stronger.

10
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

11
00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.230
You're saying you accept. then?

12
00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.240
I'm saying things have changed.

13
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.700
Raiding a handful of C-Rank dungeons
could benefit me. so I'm in.

14
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.860
Yes! Yes!

15
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.740
That's if you agree to one condition.

16
00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.330
Sure! Name whatever your
heart desires and it's yours!

17
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.370
No strike team.
Only you and I go in.

18
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.750
Uh...

19
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:43.000
You want the two of us to clear
19 C-Rank dungeons by ourselves?

20
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.620
So do we have a deal?

21
00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.630
We can't do it. Every C-Rank raid
requires a minimum of eight hunters

22
00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.010
to even step through the gate.

23
00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.890
We'll take a page out
of Dongsuk Hwang's book.

24
00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.860
Pay people to meet the quota
while we do the work.

25
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.850
I-I dunno.
It's a little too risky.

26
00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.860
So think about it this way.

27
00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.940
Fewer people going in means
less chance of casualties.

28
00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.570
and you know
we can come out unscathed.

29
00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.360
Clearing 19 dungeons
accident-free is huge.

30
00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.790
And since you're doing this to persuade your
father. wouldn't a triumph like that help?

31
00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.830
It certainly wouldn't hurt.

32
00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.260
Boss. let's do it! Nineteen raids!

33
00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.340
Okay. I'll handle arranging
gates and recruits!

34
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.640
Hmph.

35
00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.550
Hello there. sir.
Is there something you need?

36
00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.630
Very impressive.

37
00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.350
I'd expect nothing less
from an S-Rank. though.

38
00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.970
I was waiting for the right moment
to approach you. Miss Cha.

39
00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.100
Sorry to interrupt your training.

40
00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.600
But here. Please take my card.

41
00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.370
It's been over a decade
since the gates first appeared.

42
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.540
The world has changed
at a dizzying pace.

43
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.700
Infrastructure. the economy.
media. and even politics.

44
00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:48.790
The dungeons have affected all
of those in some shape or form.

45
00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.500
Take our infrastructure.

46
00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:54.850
It would appear the very foundation
of our lives can no longer operate

47
00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.010
without the resources
found in the gates.

48
00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:02.600
You hunters are the only ones able
to retrieve those resources. Jinho.

49
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.810
Then there's the Hunters Association.

50
00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:10.530
The government will continue to fund them
as long as there are hunters to be overseen.

51
00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:16.370
After all. without the Association.
who would assess the hunters?

52
00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:18.740
How would they be
ranked and registered?

53
00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:23.790
They manage gates that don't go to
auction. they handle dungeon breaks.

54
00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:28.330
And yet the Association is nothing
more than a function of the state.

55
00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.430
The ones who collect the majority
of dungeon resources

56
00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.750
to keep our economy going
are the guilds.

57
00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.010
Essentially. a business that's
been capitalizing on a market need.

58
00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:42.430
They're are extremely wealthy because
they struck while the iron was hot.

59
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.590
and it's still burning.

60
00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:49.100
Just look at the Hunters Guild. the
White Tiger Guild. the Reaper Guild.

61
00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.150
the Fame Guild.
and the Knights Guild.

62
00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.820
The five largest in the country.

63
00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.870
They have a functional monopoly
on all dungeon-related profits.

64
00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:03.990
Suits them fine. but I see no reason
we should allow that to persist.

65
00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.080
Dungeon resources
are important to everyday life.

66
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.250
Simply leaving their collection to a group
of mercenaries is out of the question.

67
00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.710
We've contributed so much
to this country. why stop now?

68
00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:17.430
We should handle
this age of dungeons. too.

69
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.680
So. we'll establish our own guild.

70
00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.090
You realize how crucial
that is. right. son?

71
00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.690
I... Yes. of course.

72
00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.560
All that may be true. but
recruiting an S-Rank hunter to act

73
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.490
as my brother's business
partner is such a dicey move.

74
00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.200
Especially. when I'm right here.

75
00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:56.550
Looks like none of the
extra reps count anymore.

76
00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:02.380
And that Cursed Random Loot Box I was offered
for that secret quest isn't available now.

77
00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.390
The system only let me
have one of the two.

78
00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.520
Man. there's a chance
I could've gotten another item

79
00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.350
as valuable
as the Demon's Castle key.

80
00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.850
But random loot boxes aren't all bad.

81
00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:19.620
I mean. the key to that instance
dungeon came from one so. maybe...

82
00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.830
M-Maybe not.

83
00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.470
With my stats as high
as they are now.

84
00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.960
three points aren't enough to
make much difference anymore.

85
00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.800
Be nice if I still had
an efficient way to level up.

86
00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.090
Those C-Rank raids will help.
but I gotta wait on Jinho.

87
00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.220
Oh. yeah! The penalty zone!

88
00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.640
I can fight that centipede and...

89
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:51.970
No.

90
00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.530
I'd have an easier time running
from that thing now. but beating it?

91
00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:59.360
And what if I don't gain experience
'cause it's a punishment?

92
00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.990
They need hunters for a D-Rank gate?

93
00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.280
The biggest pro is that it's
a good chance to level up.

94
00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:11.910
but then the con is that I'd
be fighting with a strike team.

95
00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.830
Should I pass?

96
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.470
Beggars can't be choosers.

97
00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.550
This is frustrating.

98
00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.400
You're too good.
I didn't stand a chance.

99
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.570
Sure you did.
but I'm not ready to lose.

100
00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:45.910
I wish you were still at your best. To
fight you in your prime would be an honor.

101
00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.370
Come on. it's been a few months now.

102
00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.710
When are you gonna
stop fretting over my arm?

103
00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.210
Huh?

104
00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.460
Another emergency summons.

105
00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.920
Low-ranks get a lot of these for
what amounts to running errands.

106
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.920
But you answer.
Is retiring completely out. then?

107
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.630
Me. retire?

108
00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.140
I see your point.

109
00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:14.300
Not only am I getting up there in age.
I've got a missing limb to hold me back.

110
00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.480
No! That's not what I meant. Master!

111
00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.110
Well. I only lost my arm
when I could've lost my life.

112
00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:24.310
Even though my best years are long gone.
I'd really like to spend whatever time

113
00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.540
I have left helping people out.

114
00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.800
My next raid request came in.

115
00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.210
You know. honey.

116
00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:43.920
Isn't it about time you considered
a career besides hunting?

117
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.720
-Not this again.
-It's so dangerous.

118
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.430
How many people died
in that one raid before?

119
00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:53.140
And how close were you
to dying right along with them?

120
00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.610
I guess pretty close.

121
00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.730
-Daddy! Up. up!
-Eunji.

122
00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:04.770
I hear you. but Eunji is starting preschool
and Eunha's going to middle school.

123
00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.030
-so we need the money. don't we?
-I suppose. but...

124
00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:09.240
It'll be fine.

125
00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.870
The Association makes it a point not to
send lower ranks into trickier dungeons.

126
00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.920
That one incident
was just an exception.

127
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.420
You're right. I'm sorry
for making such a fuss.

128
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.460
I get why you do. though.

129
00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.510
Please be careful. okay?

130
00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.880
Well. that's a given!
You know I love you.

131
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.680
-Hey. Daddy?
-Yeah? What's goin' on?

132
00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:33.090
Are you stwong? Like superheroes?

133
00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.390
Oh-oh. you bet I am!

134
00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.810
Your daddy can beat up the
scariest monsters you've ever seen!

135
00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:42.230
Wow! You're really.
really. really stwong. huh?

136
00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.950
You have got some damn nerve!

137
00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.070
Are you going to tell me why?

138
00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.530
Don't play dumb. You wasted my
time and stuck me with that interview!

139
00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:57.120
I caught it. by the way. You made
a very good impression. so bravo.

140
00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.460
I found your answers
both insightful and sincere.

141
00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.830
Oh. take your empty
flattery and shove it!

142
00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:05.550
You should just admit that interview
was supposed to be for you. not me!

143
00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:08.010
Well. let's recap the offer
made to Chairman Go.

144
00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:11.340
Last I checked. they wanted a
talented hunter who had great character.

145
00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.380
They also asked that
he be dedicated to his job.

146
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:18.020
With all that in mind. it doesn't
sound like they wanted me. does it?

147
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.520
Least you realize
how sketchy you are.

148
00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.850
Ah. well.

149
00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.360
It's done.
So. what's this about?

150
00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:29.650
Though I'm glad I got to tell you off. that
can't be why you asked to speak in person.

151
00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.400
Look behind you and you'll see
a detailed report about something

152
00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.570
I thought should be
brought to your attention.

153
00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:39.000
Yoojin Construction are getting
ready to launch their own guild.

154
00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:42.660
I heard. and the moves they've
been making are pretty underhanded.

155
00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:45.300
They've been headhunting at my guild.

156
00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.380
Then I suppose since
you already know.

157
00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:49.880
I have wasted your time
twice in a row now.

158
00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:55.260
Yeah. well. I already know that you knew
that I knew. so can we please cut the crap?

159
00:11:56.510 --> 00:12:00.600
I'll ask once more.
What's this really about?

160
00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.780
You haven't called lately so
I'm glad I got a hold of you.

161
00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.980
Is everything okay?

162
00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.820
-Mm-hmm.
-Work been good?

163
00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:14.280
Mm. Yeah.

164
00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.990
You've always been such
a scaredy-cat. Joohee.

165
00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.990
Makes it hard to picture
you bein' a hunter.

166
00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.200
You're B-Rank. right?

167
00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.540
I know that's supposed
to mean you're pretty strong.

168
00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.170
but wouldn't someone with
your issues just get in the way?

169
00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.950
Come on back home and
help run the family business.

170
00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:34.250
-Your daddy's worried sick...
-Look. my life isn't yours to control!

171
00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:37.350
I'm a grown woman who makes
her own choices. so just drop it!

172
00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:39.770
Where in the world is all this c--

173
00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.820
I "get in the way?"

174
00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.780
But...

175
00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.660
I wanna try just a bit longer.

176
00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.150
Pardon the intrusion.

177
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.320
Hunter Hae-in Cha. and
what can I do for you today?

178
00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.410
Nothing really. sir.

179
00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:40.280
I just wanted to let you know a scout
from Yoojin Construction offered me a job.

180
00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:41.950
Here's the card he gave me.

181
00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.740
I see.

182
00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.290
Apparently. they have plans
to launch a new guild soon.

183
00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:50.960
and were hoping I'd join them
as their guild master. so...

184
00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.420
They have good taste. but I assume
you're telling me this because you turned

185
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.890
their offer down. right?

186
00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.220
Right. Without any hesitation. sir.

187
00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.970
Thanks for your loyalty.
And honesty.

188
00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:04.680
Of course. Also. um...

189
00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:08.900
I noticed that President Baek was leaving
your office as I was on my way in. sir.

190
00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.320
May I ask what brought him here?

191
00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:22.870
I'd like to know your honest
thoughts regarding Jeju Island.

192
00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.170
Jeju Island?
Why suddenly bring that up?

193
00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:32.620
Because it should be discussed. not
sealed off and forgotten due to our failure.

194
00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.520
But only occasional reconnaissance
is done from the shore.

195
00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.340
and the public receives a single
annual update about any changes.

196
00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:41.930
People are trying to forget it all.

197
00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:45.010
To wipe the site and its
horrors from their minds.

198
00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.690
Maybe. but you can't
exactly blame them.

199
00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.060
Well. I refuse!

200
00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:52.890
No matter how commonplace gates may
have become. or how much I get fawned over

201
00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:57.650
as the "ultimate weapon" of humanity.
I will never. and I mean never.

202
00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:00.490
let the memory of Jeju slip away!

203
00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:03.650
I can't leave that island as it is.
which is why I intend to clear it

204
00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.580
in the very near future.

205
00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:09.750
And to accomplish that. I need you
and the others to be on the same page.

206
00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:15.160
We have to grow stronger. gather allies.
and sway public opinion in our favor.

207
00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:18.640
Hence the interview and
your push to train new hunters.

208
00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:29.020
I would think you'd want
to return to Jeju.

209
00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.400
Isn't there something
you left behind?

210
00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:42.120
Ah. Eunseok. Byung-gu.

211
00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.960
I'll beg you. If that's what it takes.

212
00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.170
Just please kill them.

213
00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.130
I'm heading out.

214
00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.590
I can't believe you're
working on a holiday.

215
00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.510
You sure keep busy lately.

216
00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:05.930
-Yeah. I guess.
-What universe is this?

217
00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:09.600
You used to have some downtime after
every gate because you would get injured.

218
00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.430
Is all that training paying off?

219
00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:13.220
Uh-huh. probably.

220
00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.230
In any case. I have
a stable income now.

221
00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:17.570
Be happy.

222
00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.400
Uh. okay.

223
00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:22.280
Hey. where's all your gear?
Hello?

224
00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:24.440
Don't worry about it. See ya.

225
00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:26.290
Wait. what the...?

226
00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.790
Not like it's just a trip to
the convenience store.

227
00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.210
Since my awakening didn't affect
my physical strength.

228
00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.090
my sword is useless
against magical beasts.

229
00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:45.760
The martial arts I've spent decades refining
don't really help my magic-based powers.

230
00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:50.760
A seasoned swordsman like myself becoming
a mage hunter is quite the twist of fate.

231
00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.100
Surely there's a reason for it.

232
00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:58.110
Jinwoo?

233
00:16:58.190 --> 00:16:59.860
Mister Song!

234
00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:03.110
So it is you!
Wow. I hardly recognize you!

235
00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.900
It has been a while. huh?

236
00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:07.580
What are the odds
we'd just meet on the street?

237
00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:11.700
I gotta say. though. what happened
to the gentle Jinwoo I used to know?

238
00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:14.660
It's only been a few short months.
but you're like a new man!

239
00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:19.630
Especially since I recall
you losing your right leg.

240
00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:23.960
Uh. I did. but when I woke up
in the hospital. it was still there.

241
00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.010
Well. I heard
the White Tigers found you.

242
00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:30.100
Bet you anything there was a
high-ranked healer among them!

243
00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:33.550
Whatever the case. you
have way too much life to live.

244
00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.180
so it's a relief you're healed!

245
00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:39.230
That's nice of you to say.
I wish you were. too.

246
00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:43.000
Ah. well. maybe if I had gotten
to a decent healer in time.

247
00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.400
but I've accepted it now.

248
00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:49.160
Anyway. chance meeting or not.
I'm really glad I got to see you again.

249
00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:51.660
I've been wanting to ever
since I heard you lived.

250
00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:54.450
Uh. so what brought you
to this part of town?

251
00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.630
The Association messaged me.
Said it's urgent.

252
00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:59.630
I got the message too.

253
00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.520
Hah. Now how is that
for a coincidence?

254
00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:17.570
This is quite the little reunion.

255
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:21.730
You're really here.

256
00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:25.310
Joohee. hey. Look at that.

257
00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.240
The gang's all here.

258
00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:30.570
Of course. they're ashamed.

259
00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:34.830
We escaped with our lives. but
sacrificed Jinwoo in order to do so.

260
00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:38.370
And Sang-shik also
threatened me at sword point.

261
00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.330
No wonder he can't look me
in the eye either.

262
00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:47.720
That aside. five of the six survivors
being reunited like this. makes you wonder.

263
00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.800
Oh. my gosh. This is surreal.

264
00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.840
You are Jinwoo. aren't you?

265
00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.090
I am. I swear.

266
00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.350
Your leg looks like it was
never severed and you're so tall.

267
00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:00.640
I guess you were okay
the day I came to visit.

268
00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.270
Uh. you came to visit?

269
00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:12.410
We got a fine little
lady in this group. fellas.

270
00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.750
Ditch that loser.

271
00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:18.620
Why not come get hot
and heavy with me. baby!

272
00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:22.170
-I know all kindsa games to play--
-Shut your dirty mouth.

273
00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.300
This isn't a "play date."

274
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.710
Hunters! If you step this way.

275
00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.420
I'll brief you on the unique
circumstances of your raid today.

276
00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.850
Yeah. that'd be nice.

277
00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:38.640
You all will be accompanied by
three prisoner substitute hunters

278
00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:41.770
-who are out on good behavior.
-Substitute hunters?

279
00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:44.430
You expect us
to fight alongside criminals?

280
00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.360
It's true. they are convicted men.

281
00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.940
However. they're here to reduce their
jail time so they shouldn't cause you grief.

282
00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:53.240
We've little choice in the matter
due to the shortage of local hunters.

283
00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.920
Please understand.

284
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.870
For crying out loud.

285
00:19:56.950 --> 00:20:00.900
You'll also be joined by an overseer
from the Association. Taeshik Kang.

286
00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:03.390
He's B-Rank. so even in
the worst-case scenario.

287
00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.420
he'll be able to handle
three C-Rank criminals with ease.

288
00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.300
So. you can rest assured.

289
00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.090
Something isn't right.

290
00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.340
Hey. maybe you should
sit this out. Joohee?

291
00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.470
Are you bailing. too?

292
00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.350
No. I'm going.

293
00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.310
All right. then so am I.

294
00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.320
Fair enough.

295
00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:30.820
Damn. it's good to be free.
even if we gotta work for it.

296
00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:32.570
Chainin' us like animals.

297
00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.530
You're the good guys. so why so evil?

298
00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:35.740
Shut up.

299
00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:37.740
You're chained
'cause you're convicts.

300
00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.040
And you know what happens if
you act up while the chains are off.

301
00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:49.710
As my associate previously mentioned.
I'm Taeshik Kang of the Surveillance Team.

302
00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:54.710
I'll be keeping an eye on those three
throughout the raid. so you can relax.

303
00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:58.720
We'll need a leader. though.
Do we have any volunteers?

304
00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:02.510
What do you say? Think you'd
be willing to follow my lead again?

305
00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:04.350
Of course. I would. sir.

306
00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:07.900
I appreciate you giving
me this chance.

307
00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:09.400
Uh. you don't have to bow.

308
00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:12.940
On that day. seven
people died because of me.

309
00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:16.620
The magnitude of my failure
cannot be understated.

310
00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:19.660
But six of us did make
it out. because of you.

311
00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:23.450
So let me say this
on behalf of all the survivors.

312
00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.540
I am so grateful to you.

313
00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:29.250
Mister Song. Stand up. please.

314
00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.720
Hmm.

315
00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:35.050
And what about you. Sangshik?
Do you care if I take the lead?

316
00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:39.140
If that's what you want. go ahead.

317
00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:41.180
Right.

318
00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.020
Well. it's settled.

319
00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:49.610
I volunteer to take point
in today's raid.

320
00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:52.940
Thank you for your courage.
Let's get underway then.

321
00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.750
Brace yourselves. everyone.

322
00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:05.120
Here we go.

323
00:22:06.305 --> 00:23:06.528
